                <pb facs="0526" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">438.00/226: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-26T09:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26,
                                1923—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>42. Department’s March 21, 6 [<hi rendition="#italic">5</hi>] p.m. President
                    Borno informs me he will telegraph to Monsieur Dejean today to accept French
                    proposal without reservation. He further stated that recourse to revision
                    through diplomatic channels would extend to other foreign governments having
                    claims. His interpretation is that if in proceedings of Claims Commission
                    foreign delegate files minority report disagreeing with other two delegates then
                    the foreign government [if it] so desires to [<hi rendition="#italic">may</hi>]
                    take up claim through diplomatic channels.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
